<title>USA: John Nuveen to buy back 3.5 mln shares.</title>
<headline>John Nuveen to buy back 3.5 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>John Nuveen Co said Monday it plans to repurchase up to 3.5 million of its common shares, representing slightly more than 10 percent of its outstanding common stock.</p>
<p>Nuveen said the shares will be prorated between its class A and class B shares, adding that the class B shares are owned by St. Paul Cos Inc.</p>
<p>The purchases will be made on the open market and in private transactions.</p>
<p>The company completed a previously authorized repurchase program involving 3.5 million common shares in late 1996.</p>
<p>Nuveen specializes in managed investment products and services for financial advisers and their clients.</p>
<p>Its shares closed up 1/8 Monday at 27-3/8.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
